":66}},{"item_id":"econ_tragedy_commons","prompt_name":"econ_tragedy_commons","family":"economics/econ_tragedy_commons","prior_turn_passed":null,"output":"Overgrazing","reasoning":null,"score":1,"error":null,"scorer":{"type":"constraint","constraints":[{"check":"regex","name":"matches overgrazing","pattern":"\\b[Oo][Vv][Ee][Rr][Gg][Rr][Aa][Zz][Ii][Nn][Gg]\\b"}]},"breakdown":{"passed":["matches overgrazing"],"failed":[],"errored":[]},"timing":{"wall_sec":0.471,"prompt_tokens":77,"generation_tokens":3}},{"item_id":"econ_mixed_has_pure_ne","prompt_name":"econ_mixed_has_pure_ne","family":"econ-mixed","prior_turn_passed":null,"output":"To determine if there is a pure-strategy Nash equilibrium, we need to check each cell in the payoff matrix and see if either player would have an incentive to deviate from their chosen strategy.\n\nThe payoff matrix based on the provided information is:\n\n| Server \\ Receiver | Anticipate Left | Anticipate Right |\n|-------------------|-----------------|------------------|\n| Aim Left          | (10, 2)         | (4, 8)           |\n| Aim Right         | (6, 6)          | (10, 2)          |\n\nLet's analyze each cell:\n\n1. **Aim Left, Anticipate Left (10, 2)**:\n   - Server's payoff: 10\n   - Receiver's payoff: 2\n   - If the Server deviates to Aim Right, the payoff becomes (6, 6), which is worse for the Server (10 > 6).\n   - If the Receiver deviates to Anticipate Right, the payoff becomes (4, 8), which is better for the Receiver (2 < 8).\n   - Hence, this cell is not a Nash equilibrium because the Receiver would deviate.\n\n2. **Aim Left, Anticipate Right (4, 8)**:\n   - Server's payoff: 4\n   - Receiver's payoff: 8\n   - If the Server deviates to Aim Right, the payoff becomes (10, 2), which is better for the Server (4 < 10).\n   - If the Receiver deviates to Anticipate Left, the payoff becomes (10, 2), which is worse for the Receiver (8 > 2).\n   - Hence, this cell is not a Nash equilibrium because the Server would deviate.\n\n3. **Aim Right, Anticipate Left (6, 6)**:\n   - Server's payoff: 6\n   - Receiver's payoff: 6\n   - If the Server deviates to Aim Left, the payoff becomes (10, 2), which is better for the Server (6 < 10).\n   - If the Receiver deviates to Anticipate Right, the payoff becomes (10, 2), which is worse for the Receiver (6 > 2).\n   - Hence, this cell is not a Nash equilibrium because the Server would deviate.\n\n4. **Aim Right, Anticipate Right (10, 2)**:\n   - Server's payoff: 10\n   - Receiver's payoff: 2\n   - If the Server deviates to Aim Left, the payoff becomes (4, 8), which is worse for the Server (10 > 4).\n   - If the Receiver deviates to Anticipate Left, the payoff becomes (6, 6), which is better for the Receiver (2 < 6).\n   - Hence, this cell is not a Nash equilibrium because the Receiver would deviate.\n\nSince none of the cells in the matrix are stable against unilateral deviations, this game does not have a pure-strategy Nash equilibrium.\n\n**Answer: No.**","reasoning":null,"score":1,"error":null,"scorer":{"type":"constraint","constraints":[{"check":"regex","name":"matches no","pattern":"\\b[Nn][Oo]\\b"}]},"breakdown":{"passed":["matches no"],"failed":[],"errored":[]},"timing":{"wall_sec":24.739,"prompt_tokens":173,"generation_tokens":648}},{"item_id":"econ_mixed_server_prob_left","prompt_name":"econ_mixed_server_prob_left","family":"econ-mixed","prior_turn_passed":null,"output":"0.8","reasoning":null,"score":0,"error":null,"scorer":{"type":"constraint","constraints":[{"check":"regex","name":"equals 0.4","pattern":"(?<![\\d.])0?\\.40*(?!\\d)"}],"nearMisses":[{"slip":"percent-for-decimal","credit":0.5,"pattern":"(?<![\\d.])40(?:\\.0*)?\\s*%"}]},"breakdown":{"passed":[],"failed":["equals 0.4"],"errored":[]},"timing":{"wall_sec":0.639,"prompt_tokens":178,"generation_tokens":3}},{"item_id":"econ_mixed_receiver_prob_left","prompt_name":"econ_mixed_receiver_prob_left","family":"econ-mixed","prior_turn_passed":null,"output":"0.5","reasoning":null,"score":0,"error":nul